@@ -107,6 +107,7 @@ Bugs
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Huebner2017`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Huebner2018`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Liu2024` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Sosulski2019` no longer download the Zenodo ``subjectXX.zip`` / figshare ``edffile.zip`` / FreiDok archive when NEMAR (``nm000199``, ``nm000195``, ``nm000158``, ``nm000266``) or an earlier extraction already holds the files they read: ``data_path`` now looks for the extracted subject directory (Huebner, Sosulski2019) or EDF (Liu2024) first, through :func:`moabb.datasets.download.fill_from_store` and the new :func:`moabb.datasets.download.fill_tree_from_store`, which places a whole extracted directory from the store and refuses one whose BrainVision/EEGLAB headers name files the store lacks. Liu2024 now extracts only the archive members not on disk yet, so a later extraction does not write through the links into the NEMAR store, and Sosulski2019 extracts the archive again when a subject's inner ZIP is missing instead of whenever ``extracted/`` is absent (:gh:`1293` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`~moabb.datasets.Nieto2022` and :class:`~moabb.datasets.TrianaGuzman2024` declared their NEMAR raw mirrors (``on003626``, ``on005342``) but always downloaded from OpenNeuro's S3 bucket; like the other OpenNeuro loaders they now read the mirror first under the ``"auto"`` and ``"nemar"`` providers and keep OpenNeuro as the fallback and for ``"upstream"`` (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`~moabb.datasets.Chailloux2020`, :class:`~moabb.datasets.Nieto2022` and :class:`~moabb.datasets.TrianaGuzman2024` declared their NEMAR raw mirrors (``on003190``, ``on003626``, ``on005342``) but always downloaded from OpenNeuro's S3 bucket; like the other OpenNeuro loaders they now read the mirror first under the ``"auto"`` and ``"nemar"`` providers and keep OpenNeuro as the fallback and for ``"upstream"`` (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- :class:`moabb.datasets.HefmiIch2025` and :class:`moabb.datasets.AguileraRodriguez2025` read what their NEMAR deposits (``nm000347``, ``nm000174``) hold instead of asking figshare/Mendeley again. HefmiIch2025 fetched its figshare file list with a bare ``requests.get`` on ``api.figshare.com``; it now caches it as ``figshare_filelist_28955456.json`` (like the MAMEM loaders), takes it from the deposit's ``sourcedata/`` when present, else from :func:`moabb.datasets.download.fs_get_file_list`, and downloads each epoch file under its local name so the store serves it. The URL lookup of :func:`moabb.datasets.download.data_dl` also accepts a stored file that only adds an extension to an extension-less URL name (exactly one candidate, two or more path segments): the AguileraRodriguez2025 deposit keeps Mendeley's ``<uuid>/file_downloaded`` as ``file_downloaded.edf``/``.xdf`` (:gh:`1295` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Peterson2020` loads again with the default ``"auto"`` download provider: the NEMAR mirror (``on003810``) ships the BIDS ``events.tsv`` sidecars, so ``read_raw_bids`` replaced the EDF's ``OVTK_GDF_Right``/``OVTK_GDF_Tongue`` annotations with the sidecar values ``7``/``9`` and every load stopped with ``ValueError: Could not find any of the events you specified``. Both codings now map to ``motor_imagery``/``rest`` (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix every :class:`moabb.datasets.Thapa2025` load failing with "The header file must be given to read the data, not a file with extension '.eeg'": ``data_path`` listed the runs with :func:`mne_bids.find_matching_paths` without an extension filter, so it returned each run's ``_eeg.eeg`` and ``_eeg.vmrk`` beside its ``_eeg.vhdr`` and ``read_raw_brainvision`` was handed the binary file. It now returns the ``.vhdr`` headers only; this affected both the Figshare archive and the NEMAR ``nm000324`` copy (:gh:`1292` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - With the default ``"auto"`` download provider, 28 datasets whose loader caches files under names their download URLs do not carry no longer re-download from the upstream host what NEMAR already served: NEMAR deposits are snapshots of the loader's own cache (extracted archives, files named after figshare/Dataverse/Mendeley ids), which the URL-tail lookup of :func:`moabb.datasets.download.data_dl` cannot match. With the new class attribute ``nemar_seed_cache = True``, :meth:`~moabb.datasets.base.BaseDataset.get_data` links the subject's prefetched store files into the loader cache at the location the deposit's provenance records (``upstream_cache_root``), using the new :func:`moabb.datasets.download.seed_loader_cache`; recordings whose headers name files the deposit lacks (BrainVision, EEGLAB, Curry) are not placed. Seeding is opt-in because a loader that skips its download once anything is cached would load less data from an incomplete deposit (seen for Lee2021Mobile and BI2013a); it is enabled for the loaders an audit of every ``nemar_id`` verified to load the same runs from NEMAR alone: Batista2022, Beetl2021_A/B, Farabbi2020, GuttmannFlury2025_ME/MI/P300, Han2024Fatigue, Jia2019, Kaya2018, Liu2020BETA, Liu2022EldBETA, Ma2020, MILimbEEG, Mainsah2025 (all studies; the EDF list still comes from PhysioNet's ``SHA256SUMS.txt``), Nguyen2017_S/SL, Ortiz2023, PoloHortiguela2025, Pressel2016, RomaniBF2025ERP, Rozado2015, Simoes2020, Speier2017, Wairagkar2018, Wang2021Combined, Zhang2017 and Zuo2025 (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
